I have finally finished my mac nethack port.  I'll post it to
comp.mac.binaries on Monday, and assuming that the moderator passes it
on, it should appear there soon.  If you don't have access to that
newsgroup, I'll E-mail you a copy if I can.  If there are many
requests and comp.binaries.mac doesn't take it, I suppose I could post
it here; I don't know if that would be kosher, though, as it takes
about 600K; could somebody fill me in?.  In any case, I will make it
available for anon ftp via whitechapel.media.mit.edu (18.85.0.125),
also by Monday.  I believe it to be essentially bug-free (or at least
as bug-free as the unix/PC versions). A description follows.

	This is Mac Nethack, ported from version 3.0f, patchlevel 3. 
It is essentially the same as the unix/PC nethack, with all features
included (except MAIL).  It features a dialog box for setting the player
name and options, which can be saved.  It also has multi-colored
monsters (for those of you running on color machines) and a special
9x15 font which some of you may have seen before in X windows, so
the walls and the monsters appear as unique glyphs, not letters. 
Save/restore seems to work reliably (unlike the 2.3 port which some
of you may have played).  It weighs in at about 560K for the
application, plus some data files, which you can place in a sub-folder
called "lib", if you like, or in the same folder as the application.  It will
run under multifinder.  I have only tested this with color and
monochrome mac II's with 2 megs of RAM, but the "clover" shift key
generates control characters, so it ought to run on macs with wimpy
keyboards, and the apllication is small enough that it should run in 1
meg.  The only new bug (i.e. aside from those known about in
patchlevel 3) that I know of is occasionally miscoloring walls and
monsters: you can think of this as a multi-racial and/or decorative
feature. I do.



	Anyway, enjoy it and send me mail if you like it: it's
freeware and should not be sold.  If you edit the font (use ResEdit)
and come up with some nice new character glyphs, send me a copy!



-Mike Sokolov


